        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31-a5">

                <pb facs="0708" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv08/pg698"/>

                <head>Appendix B to HD–72</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-17">October 17, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Telegram</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">From: Interallied Military Commission.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To: Supreme Council, Peace Conference, Paris.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 841</p>
                <p>The Commission has just learned, through a telegram addressed to one of its
                    members, of the early arrival at Budapest of Sir George Clerk, supplied with
                    full powers. It requests that this designation be officially confirmed by the
                    Supreme Council and to clearly specify just what shall be the respective
                    attributions of the Commission on one hand, and of Sir George Clerk on the
                    other.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
